    <solution><m>{\left(\frac{x}{7}\right)}^{2}-{\left(\frac{y}{8}\right)}^{2}=1</m>. For this hyperbola,
<m>a=7</m>, <m>b=8</m> and
<m>c=\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{8}^{2}}\approx 10.630</m>.


 Hence,  the foci are at
<m>\left(10.630, 0\right)</m> and
<m>\left(-10.630, 0\right)</m>

 and the vertices are at
<m>\left(7, 0\right)</m> and
<m>\left(-7, 0\right)</m>. 

 Since the given hyperbola is obtained by translating the center of the hyperbola
<m>{\left(\frac{x}{7}\right)}^{2}-{\left(\frac{y}{8}\right)}^{2}=1</m>  to the point
<m>\left( + 9, -2\right)</m>, 

 the foci are at
<m>{F}_{1}=\left(10.630 + 9, 0-2\right)=\left(19.630, -2\right)</m> and
<m>{F}_{2}=\left(-10.630 + 9, 0-2\right)=\left(-1.630, -2\right)</m> 

 and the vertices are
<m>A=(7 + 9, 0-2)=(16, -2)</m> and
<m>{A}^{\prime }=(-7 + 9, 0-2)=(2, -2)</m>.



</solution>
